  "body": "The [battery status API](https://w3c.github.io/battery/#dom-navigator-getbattery) wants to create a restriction to be used in top-level browsing contexts.\r\n\r\nAs I mentioned in https://github.com/w3c/battery/issues/19, the correct way to formalize this appears to be something like:\r\n\r\n> If this Navigator object's [relevant global object](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-relevant-global)'s [associated Document](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-window)'s [browsing context](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-bc) is a top-level browsing context...\r\n\r\nWe could create some shorthand definitions here that allow us to reduce this to\r\n\r\n> If this Navigator object's [relevant browsing context] is a top-level browsing context...\r\n\r\n(This definition would only be meaningful for platform objects whose relevant global object is a Window.)\r\n\r\nWe could also do the same for \"current\", mainly for use in constructors. (Just using the current global object, instead of the relevant one.)\r\n\r\nI'm filing this as a tracking issue to see if we encounter other cases that would benefit from such a definition. There may be some in the HTML Standard already; I haven't checked exhaustively. But I mainly wanted a place to consolidate future instances we find.",
